1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:07,500
Why ECN-2 Film Lab Costs Are Rising in 2026. Silver, chemistry supply and what a lab can control

2
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:18,595
ECN-2 lab costs are rising because film is built on silver and the chemistry behind developer, bleach and fixer comes from a concentrated supply chain.

3
00:00:18,595 --> 00:00:28,489
Silver passed US$80 an ounce for the first time in late December 2025, after more than doubling during the year. A lab cannot move the silver price.

4
00:00:28,489 --> 00:00:32,500
It can control how much of each run becomes usable negative.

5
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:39,227
Silver set a series of record highs in December 2025 and briefly traded above US$80 an ounce.

6
00:00:39,227 --> 00:00:49,571
Kodak Alaris raised prices on its distributed film stocks by US$1 to US$3 a roll from 1 February 2026. Film is estimated to cost around three times what it did in 2016.

7
00:00:49,571 --> 00:00:58,500
Movement is uneven by market: one 2026 survey found an average rise of about 2.5% over six months. Sources: Kitco News; PhotoWorkout; Analog Cafe

8
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:06,669
Factor: Silver price. Can a lab control it?: No. What helps: Plan processing around a calendar. Factor: Chemistry supply chain. Can a lab control it?: No.

9
00:01:06,669 --> 00:01:14,398
What helps: Order developer and fixer ahead of need. Factor: Developer temperature. Can a lab control it?: Yes. What helps: Hold the Z-119 setpoint of 41.1°C (106°F).

10
00:01:14,398 --> 00:01:22,033
Factor: Agitation and replenishment. Can a lab control it?: Yes. What helps: Keep both consistent between runs. Factor: Reject runs. Can a lab control it?: Largely.

11
00:01:22,033 --> 00:01:24,500
What helps: Fewer rerun batches waste less chemistry.

12
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:33,088
A dedicated ECN-2 processor is designed around the Kodak Z-119 process, with temperature control and replenishment set up for it.

13
00:01:33,088 --> 00:01:41,324
Converted C-41 minilabs and hand-agitated drums were not designed for ECN-2. Keeping them in specification can take more operator attention.

14
00:01:41,324 --> 00:01:45,500
Results depend on the equipment, the operator and the volume processed.

15
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:55,251
1. Silver price: does the late-2025 rally hold or unwind?. 2. Film maker changes: do investment and distribution shifts steady prices?. 3.

16
00:01:55,251 --> 00:01:59,500
Chemistry lead times: plan orders against your processing calendar.

17
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:09,295
Is the chemistry problem specific to ECN-2? No. Supply pressure affects photographic chemistry generally, and ECN-2 chemistry sits in the same market.

18
00:02:09,295 --> 00:02:18,500
Will costs come back down? No one can say. Some commentators called the silver rally speculative, but chemistry sourcing is a separate, longer-running issue.

